# Git remotes — GitHub primary, owner-only authors, GitLab on demand

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/ronanop/enterprise-erp.git` | **Primary** — fetch + default push |
| `iconnectplus` | `https://github.com/Moksh-CacheDigitech/iConnectPlus.git` | Always-synced mirror |
| `iconnectplus-erp` | `https://github.com/moksh-sharma/iConnectPlus-ERP.git` | Always-synced mirror |
| `gitlab` | `https://172.16.200.77/cachedigitech/cache-erp-vapt-31-aug.git` | Mirror — only on explicit request |

GitHub `origin` is the source of truth for **content**. All three GitHub remotes must keep **owner-only commit attribution**:

- Author / committer: **Moksh Sharma** `<moksh-sharma@users.noreply.github.com>`

Do **not** leave multi-author history on `origin`, `iconnectplus`, or `iconnectplus-erp`.

**Settings scope:** sync **code/refs only** to mirrors — never sync collaborators, teams, or other GitHub repo settings.

## When the user asks to push / push to git

1. Commit on the current branch as usual.
2. Sync **owner-rewritten** history to all GitHub remotes (force-push as needed):

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1
```

That script rewrites author/committer to the owner, force-pushes `origin` (+ its push URLs), `iconnectplus`, and `iconnectplus-erp`, then resets local `main` to the rewritten tip.

3. Do **not** plain `git push origin` alone if that would publish multi-author commits — prefer the script above after any push-to-git request.
4. Do **not** push GitLab unless explicitly asked.

## When the user asks to sync iconnectplus / iconnectplus-erp / keep remotes synced

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/sync-iconnectplus-erp.ps1
```

## When the user asks to sync gitlab

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push gitlab HEAD:<branch> --force-with-lease
```

(After an owner rewrite, `origin` tip already matches local; push GitLab to that tip.)

Prefer matching branch names. Owner-history sync uses `--force` by design on the GitHub remotes.

This GitLab host uses a self-signed cert. Local repo already has `http.https://172.16.200.77/.sslVerify=false`. Auth requires a GitLab username + PAT; ask the user if push fails.

## Do not

- Leave or re-introduce multi-author history on `origin` / `iconnectplus` / `iconnectplus-erp`
- Skip the owner-rewrite sync on "push to git"
- Sync collaborators / GitHub settings onto mirrors
- Auto-sync GitLab on every GitHub push
- Treat mirrors as primary fetch when the user said "push to git"
- Sync mirrors → origin unless the user explicitly asks
